The comment `@@@ If the list originally contained the element, the method returns true.` indicates that the return value (`\result`) should be `true` if the element was present in the list before the method execution.

To express this, we check whether the list contained the element `o` before the call using `\old(this.contains(o))`. If that was the case, then the method should return `true`.

Thus, the assertion is:

<code>assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true;</code>
